<section class="sec" aria-labelledby="scope-h">
<div class="container">
<div class="sec-head"><h2 id="scope-h">Scope, plainly stated.</h2></div>
<div class="fit">
<div class="fit-col fit-yes">
<h3>Well suited to</h3>
<ul>
<li>Sensory processing differences affecting daily participation</li>
<li>Feeding and mealtime difficulties with a sensory or behavioral component, including very restricted diets</li>
<li>Self-regulation, coping, and escalation patterns at home</li>
<li>Foundational play and early communication, particularly birth to three</li>
<li>Fine motor development and daily-living skills</li>
<li>Social skill development in older children</li>
<li>Home safety and environmental set-up</li>
<li>Families waiting on diagnostic assessment or an early intervention place who need something now</li>
<li>Parent and caregiver coaching, with or without the child in direct sessions</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="fit-col fit-no">
<h3>Not the right referral for</h3>
<ul>
<li>Formal diagnostic evaluation — I don't diagnose</li>
<li>Children whose therapy depends on specialized clinic equipment as its core</li>
<li>Speech-language or physical therapy needs (happy to redirect)</li>
<li>Families who need services billed directly to insurance — a clinic in network will cost them less</li>
<li>Acute medical or mental health crisis</li>
<li><span class="todo-inline">[Julia to confirm any further exclusions — e.g. specific medical complexity, feeding tubes, post-surgical rehab.]</span></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<div class="note-block mt">
<h3>Conditions and profiles</h3>
<p>I've worked with children across a wide range of neurodevelopmental, genetic and medical profiles, including autistic children, children with ADHD, global and specific developmental delay, genetic conditions, prematurity, and children with no diagnosis at all. My practice is neuroaffirmative — goals are framed around participation and wellbeing rather than around presenting as neurotypical, and I don't work on suppressing stimming or enforcing eye contact.</p>
<p>Because I don't require a diagnosis to begin, a referral doesn't need to wait on one.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec sec-alt tint-blue" aria-labelledby="refer-h">
<div class="container split">
<div class="split-head"><h2 id="refer-h">How to refer.</h2></div>
<div class="split-body">
<ol class="plain-ol">
<li><b>Give the family my details.</b> That's genuinely enough — no form, no referral letter, no authorization. They book a free {{ site.introCall.minutes }}-minute call and we work out whether it's a fit.</li>
<li><b>Or contact me first</b> if you'd rather check the fit before raising it with them. Quicker for everyone if it turns out I'm not the right person.</li>
<li><b>If you'd like a summary back</b>, tell the family to mention you when they call, or send me a note yourself, so I know where to write.</li>
</ol>
<p class="small-note">Useful but never required: what prompted the referral, what's already been tried, who else is involved, and anything the family has already been told.</p>

