<div class="container">
<div class="sec-head">
<h2 id="consult-h">Consulting for childcare providers, programs and classrooms.</h2>
<p>Working with a setting rather than an individual child — for staff who have a child they're struggling to support, or who want to make a room work better for everyone in it.</p>
</div>
<div class="grid2">
<div class="card">
<h3>What it can cover</h3>
<p>Environmental assessment of a room — noise, light, layout, transitions, storage. Routines and schedule structure. Sensory strategies a whole group can use. Specific support around one child, with family consent. Staff coaching on reading and responding to escalation.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<h3>How it works</h3>
<p>Usually an initial visit to observe the setting in ordinary operation, then written suggestions and a follow-up. Ongoing arrangements are possible where that's more useful than a one-off.</p>
<p class="caveat">Fees: <span class="todo-inline">[program / classroom consulting rate — confirm whether this differs from the ${{ site.services[1].price }} family consulting rate]</span></p>
